fpcmoh: add support for FPC 10a5:a900 (Honor MagicBook)

The a900 is an FPC "Disum" match-on-host sensor, firmware 22.26.2.29. It is
the same protocol family as the already-supported 9800: one bulk IN endpoint
(0x82), all host->device traffic on EP0 as vendor control transfers, and a
TLS-PSK session whose PSK identity on the wire is literally "Disum PSK".
libfpcbep.so's key material handshakes with it unmodified.

Both entries are kept -- this adds the a900, it does not replace the 9800.

The probe switch gains a matching case purely so the device does not log
"Device a900 is not supported". Both arms set max_enroll_stage to the same
value, so this is cosmetic; probe completed successfully either way.

Applies on top of merge request 396.
---
--- a/libfprint/drivers/fpcmoh/fpc.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/fpcmoh/fpc.c
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@
 
 static const FpIdEntry id_table[] = {
   { .vid = 0x10A5,  .pid = 0x9800,  },
+  { .vid = 0x10A5,  .pid = 0xA900,  },   /* Honor MagicBook, FPC "Disum", FW 22.26.2.29 */
   { .vid = 0,  .pid = 0,  .driver_data = 0 },   /* terminating entry */
 };
 
@@ -1458,6 +1459,7 @@
   switch (productid)
     {
     case 0x9800:
+    case 0xA900:
       self->max_enroll_stage = MAX_ENROLL_SAMPLES;
       break;
 
